<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- HERO -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<header class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="overline">Academy Awards Historical Analysis</div>
    <h1>Nine Decades of Oscar-Winning Scores</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      A comprehensive analysis of every Academy Award for Best Original Score,
      tracing composer dominance, stylistic evolution, and historical patterns
      across 93 ceremonies from 1934 through 2026.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">Compiled May 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Data: All Oscar Soundtracks Dataset (Kaggle/ActarusLab)</p>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 1: OVERVIEW -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="overview">
  <div class="container">

    <!-- KPI Cards -->
    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value">79</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Total Unique Composers</div>
        <div class="kpi-note">across all 93 ceremonies</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value">4</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Max Wins by a Single Composer</div>
        <div class="kpi-note">three-way tie (Williams, Barry, Göransson)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value">28.0%</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Repeat Winner Rate</div>
        <div class="kpi-note">26 of 93 ceremonies</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi-card">
        <div class="kpi-value">12</div>
        <div class="kpi-label">Most Unique Winners / Decade</div>
        <div class="kpi-note">tie: 1940s &amp; 1980s</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-overline">Section 1</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Dataset Overview &amp; Historical Context</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This report analyzes every winner of the Academy Award for Best Original Score
        from the <strong>6th Academy Awards ceremony in 1934</strong> through the
        <strong>98th ceremony in March 2026</strong> — a span of <span class="stat-inline">93 consecutive ceremonies</span>.
        The dataset consolidates one winner per year, even for periods when the Academy
        briefly split the category into sub-awards (e.g., dramatic vs. comedy/musical scores).
      </p>
      <p>
        Across these 93 ceremonies, <span class="stat-inline">79 distinct composers</span> have claimed
        the award. Some entries credit multiple composers — eight ceremonies recognized collaborative
        scores, including the four-composer team behind <em>Stagecoach</em> (1939) and the three-composer
        collaboration on <em>Soul</em> (2020). When accounting for these shared wins, the total number of
        individual composer-recipient instances is 106 across the 93 ceremonies.
      </p>
      <p>
        The category has undergone significant evolution. Originally called "Best Scoring," it has been
        known variously as Best Original Score, Best Original Dramatic Score, and Best Original Musical
        or Comedy Score during periods of split-category experimentation. The dataset normalizes this
        history into one canonical winner per year, enabling clean longitudinal analysis.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 2: TOP COMPOSERS -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="top-composers">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-overline">Section 2</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Most Awarded Composers</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Three composers share the record with four wins each. Another four have won three times,
      and sixteen composers have won twice. Half of all winning composers (40 of 79) have won
      exactly once — underscoring how difficult repeat victories are in this category.
    </p>

    <div class="chart-row">
      <div class="chart-container tall">
        <div class="chart-title">Top Composers by Oscar Wins</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Composers with 2+ Best Original Score wins (click labels to toggle)</div>
        <canvas id="composerChart"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-container tall">
        <div class="chart-title">Win Distribution</div>
        <div class="chart-subtitle">Share of all ceremonies by win count bracket</div>
        <canvas id="winDistChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <table class="composer-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>#</th>
          <th>Composer</th>
          <th>Wins</th>
          <th>Winning Years</th>
          <th>Era</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="rank">1</td><td class="name">John Williams</td><td class="wins">4</td><td class="years">1975, 1977, 1982, 1993</td><td><span class="era">Silver–Modern</span></td></tr>
